        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: The Kabalas\n- Places: Quad Cities, American Mid-West, Europe, the Americas\n- Concepts: Klezmer, Jewish folksongs, Israeli popular songs, Polka, popular music, Czech dance, dance music\n\nFacts:\n- The Kabalas were a four-piece band from the Quad Cities area of the American Mid-West.\n- The Kabalas based their music firmly in a traditional Eastern European Klezmer style.\n- The Kabalas mixed Jewish folksongs, Israeli popular songs, Polka, and popular music into their musical style.\n- Polka is originally a Czech dance and a genre of dance music.\n- Polka is familiar throughout Europe and the Americas.",
